From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] video: sunxi: support VIDEO_COPY

The display engine scans the framebuffer U-Boot draws into. A redraw of
the whole screen, such as the configuration editor's (cedit) on every
key press, first fills the screen with the background and then draws the
scene. At 800x480x4 the fill is 1.5 MiB, far more than the ARM926's
16 KiB data cache, so most of it reaches DRAM before the scene is drawn
and the panel shows the blank screen in between: the form flickers on
every key.

Support VIDEO_COPY: reserve a second buffer of the same size, let the
display scan that one, and let video_sync() copy only the finished,
changed area into it. Without VIDEO_COPY nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/video/sunxi/sunxi_display.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/video/sunxi/sunxi_display.c
+++ b/drivers/video/sunxi/sunxi_display.c
@@ -1215,7 +1215,15 @@
 	       sunxi_get_mon_desc(sunxi_display->monitor),
 	       overscan_x, overscan_y);
 
-	sunxi_display->fb_addr = plat->base;
+	/*
+	 * With VIDEO_COPY, U-Boot draws into plat->base and video_sync()
+	 * copies the finished, changed area into plat->copy_base, so the
+	 * display must scan the copy: it then never shows a half-drawn frame.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_COPY) && plat->copy_base)
+		sunxi_display->fb_addr = plat->copy_base;
+	else
+		sunxi_display->fb_addr = plat->base;
 	sunxi_engines_init();
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_EFI_LOADER
@@ -1259,6 +1267,10 @@
 		plat->size = LCD_MAX_WIDTH * LCD_MAX_HEIGHT *
 			     VNBYTES(LCD_MAX_LOG2_BPP);
 
+	/* A second buffer of the same size for the display to scan */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_COPY))
+		plat->copy_size = plat->size;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
